{
  "id": "making-ai-work",
  "name": "Making AI Work",
  "source": "https://enterpriseai.economictimes.indiatimes.com/making-ai-work",
  "briefReady": true,
  "briefCategory": "enterprise AI leadership",

  "shared": ["et-global.css", "et-animate.css", "et-platform.css"],
  "fonts": [
    "https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@100;200;300;400;500;600;700;800&display=swap",
    "https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@200;300;400;500;600;700;800&display=swap"
  ],
  "theme": "theme.css",
  "design": {
    "notes": "What the editor's theme controls act on. headingFontVar = the variable most headings read — unlike TECH500 this design has no separate '-v2' variant, every heading reads --heading-font-family (Plus Jakarta Sans) directly, already set on <body>. headings/buttons/cards = selectors for the heading, corner-radius controls. swatches = theme colours offered besides the template's own.",
    "headingFontVar": "--heading-font-family",
    "headings": ".page_hdng4 h2, .page_hdng4 h1, .page_hdng2 h2",
    "buttons": "a.book-btn",
    "cards": ".who-enter-box li, .key-topic-card, .conventions-wdgt li, .news-card, .gridPadItem, .contacts .contact-box-wrapper .contact-box",
    "swatches": ["#186BF9", "#002156", "#000000", "#FFFFFF", "#9FCDFF"]
  },
  "editorFonts": {
    "Geist": "Geist, Arial, sans-serif",
    "Plus Jakarta Sans": "\"Plus Jakarta Sans\", Arial, sans-serif"
  },

  "body": {
    "id": "enterpriseai",
    "class": "microsite product_microsite heading-style-3 color_white web_view_ et_enterpriseai",
    "classNotes": "single-header is added at runtime by ET's header script on the live page, same as TECH500.",
    "style": {
      "--default-color": "rgb(25 27 31)",
      "--bg-color": "rgba(0, 14, 38, 1)",
      "--bg-spacing": "14px 0",
      "--para-font-size": "18px",
      "--theme-color": "rgba(24, 107, 249, 1)",
      "--primary-font-size": "40px",
      "--secondary-font-size": "16px",
      "--body-color": "rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)",
      "font-size": "16px",
      "--nav-text-color": "rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)",
      "--nav-bg-color": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)",
      "--body-font-family": "Geist, Arial, sans-serif",
      "--heading-font-family": "Plus Jakarta Sans, Arial, sans-serif",
      "--heading-color": "rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)"
    }
  },

  "content": {
    "notes": "How Create Event's content fills this template (editor-fill.js has the rule reference). from = a Create Event library id (step 3) or event (step 1). Two sections needed new LIBRARY entries added to create-event.html because nothing existing fit their real, event-specific content: 'key-topic' (the live page's own 'Key Discussion Points' graphic) is a verbatim match for the EXISTING 'priorities' library (same name, same shape) — no new entry needed there, just reused it. 'who-enter' ('Four Questions the Enterprise Now Has to Answer') had no existing fit, so a new 'keyquestions' library entry (shape 'columns', same t/d fields) was added. Both are genuine, event-specific content, not publisher boilerplate, so neither was left static. 'glimpses_event' (the gallery) maps to the 'glimpses' library and to the event's gallery records (Content › Gallery): one tile per photo, linked to itself, its caption over it; the live page's five columns of two are one flat wall here so a list rule can draw it, and with no photos the section is not on the live site. 'about-wrapper' (the 'Making AI Work' Manifesto) is left out of content.map entirely and deliberately: it's the publisher's own brand statement, the same copy regardless of which 'Making AI Work' event is running, exactly like TECH500's 'About ETCIO' — not event content a wizard field should own. The banner names the event in words (its headline, or its name) with the tagline under it; an event with a logo shows the logo instead. Speaker cards show each speaker's own photo, name, role and company (Content › Speakers); the section file holds one neutral model card, and a speaker without a photo gets the shared grey avatar. Contacts are the event's records too (Content › Contact). The banner's one picture, img.banner-bg-image, is replaced by the event's own banner (an uploaded image or a PSD's flattened image), and a video plays over it only when the event supplies a video file of its own, same as TECH500.",
    "bindNotes": "Elements that show one of the event's own details (Content › Basics) and follow it on every visit (rv-data.js, data-rv-bind). The section files carry the attribute themselves; this list is for pages saved before they did.",
    "bind": [
      { "section": "banner", "sel": "img.logo", "bind": "event.logo" },
      { "section": "banner", "sel": ".icn-box:has(.bi-calendar3)", "bind": "event.date" },
      { "section": "banner", "sel": ".icn-box:has(.bi-geo-alt)", "bind": "event.venue" }
    ],
    "map": [
      { "from": "hero", "section": "banner",
        "aiSkipMedia": "img.banner-bg-image",
        "fill": [
        { "attr": "img.banner-bg-image", "name": "src", "value": "{hero.bannerUrl}", "empty": "keep" },
        { "bgvideo": ".bnr-bg-video", "value": "{hero.video.url}", "poster": "img.banner-bg-image" },
        { "attr": "img.logo", "name": "src", "value": "{event.logo}" },
        { "attr": "img.logo", "name": "alt", "value": "{event.name}" },
        { "show": "img.logo", "if": "{event.logo}" },
        { "text": ".banner-title", "value": "{hero.title|event.name}", "bind": "event.name" },
        { "text": ".banner-tagline", "value": "{hero.tagline}", "empty": "remove" },
        { "text": ".icn-box:has(.bi-calendar3)", "value": "{event.dateLabel|event.date}", "empty": "remove" },
        { "text": ".icn-box:has(.bi-geo-alt)", "value": "{event.location}", "empty": "remove" },
        { "text": ".btn-wrapper .book-btn:not(.btn-outline)", "value": "{hero.cta1}", "empty": "keep" },
        { "text": ".btn-wrapper .book-btn.btn-outline", "value": "{hero.cta2}", "empty": "remove" }
      ] },
      { "from": "about", "section": "overview",
        "intro": { "heading": "h2", "body": ".second_content > p", "media": { "sel": ".ovr-img", "wrap": "col-md-7 ovr-img" } },
        "fill": [] },
      { "from": "keyquestions", "section": "who-enter",
        "fill": [
        { "list": ".who-enter-box ul.first > li", "items": "keyquestions.items", "require": "{t}{d}", "empty": "hide", "fill": [
          { "text": "h4", "value": "{t}" },
          { "text": "p", "value": "{d}" }
        ] }
      ] },
      { "from": "priorities", "section": "key-topic",
        "intro": { "heading": { "sel": "h2", "skip": "span" } },
        "fill": [
        { "list": ".key-topic-card", "items": "priorities.items", "require": "{t}{d}", "empty": "hide", "fill": [
          { "text": "h3", "value": "{t}" },
          { "text": "p", "value": "{d}" }
        ] }
      ] },
      { "from": "speakers", "section": "our-speakers",
        "intro": { "heading": "h2" },
        "fill": [
        { "list": ".gridPadItem", "items": "speakers.items", "require": "{n}", "empty": "hide", "fill": [
          { "attr": "img", "name": "src", "value": "{photo}", "empty": "keep" },
          { "attr": "img", "name": "alt", "value": "{n}" },
          { "text": "h5", "value": "{n}" },
          { "text": "span", "value": "{r+c:', '}", "empty": "remove" }
        ] }
      ] },
      { "from": "whyjoin", "section": "fact-marquee",
        "intro": { "heading": "h2" },
        "fill": [
        { "list": ".news-card", "items": "whyjoin.items", "require": "{t}{d}", "empty": "hide", "fill": [
          { "text": ".content h3", "value": "{d|t}" }
        ] }
      ] },
      { "from": "attend", "section": "conventions-box",
        "intro": { "subheading": "h2 > span", "heading": { "sel": "h2", "skip": "span" }, "body": ".page_hdng4.text-style > p" },
        "fill": [
        { "list": ".conventions-wdgt ul.first > li", "items": "attend.items", "require": "{t}{d}", "empty": "hide", "fill": [
          { "text": "h3", "value": "{t}" },
          { "text": "p", "value": "{d}" }
        ] }
      ] },
      { "from": "glimpses", "section": "glimpses_event",
        "intro": { "heading": "h2" },
        "fill": [
        { "list": ".glimpses-grid > .images__link", "items": "glimpses.items", "require": "{url}", "empty": "hide", "fill": [
          { "attr": ":self", "name": "href", "value": "{url}" },
          { "attr": "img", "name": "src", "value": "{url}" },
          { "attr": "img", "name": "alt", "value": "{caption}" },
          { "text": ".glimpse-caption", "value": "{caption}", "empty": "remove" }
        ] }
      ] },
      { "from": "contact", "section": "contact-us", "fill": [
        { "list": ".flex-width-auto > .col-md-4", "items": "contact.blocks", "empty": "hide", "fill": [
          { "text": ".line-1", "value": "{t}", "empty": "remove" },
          { "list": ".contact-box", "items": "people", "empty": "hide", "fill": [
            { "text": ".name", "value": "{n}", "empty": "remove" },
            { "text": "a.email", "value": "{e}", "empty": "remove:span.email" },
            { "attr": "a.email", "name": "href", "value": "mailto:{e}" },
            { "text": "a.phone", "value": "{p}", "empty": "remove:span.phone" },
            { "attr": "a.phone", "name": "href", "value": "tel:{p}" }
          ] }
        ] }
      ] }
    ]
  },

  "layout": {
    "notes": "Which sections an event's own narrative order can touch. pinStart/pinEnd never move — the hero always opens the page and Contact/the Manifesto publisher block always close it, matching the live site and the same spirit as TECH500's own pinEnd. Everything else is free for RevampCanvas.mount()'s sectionOrder option to resequence.",
    "pinStart": ["banner"],
    "pinEnd": ["contact-us", "about-wrapper"]
  },

  "sectionsNotes": "repeat = the section's repeating cards for the editor's Layout items: item = selector for one card (its parent is the list), label = what the list shows for it.",
  "sections": [
    { "id": "banner",         "name": "Banner",                          "etId": null,     "widget": "et-banner" },
    { "id": "overview",       "name": "Overview",                        "etId": null },
    { "id": "who-enter",      "name": "Questions this raises",           "etId": null,     "repeat": { "item": ".who-enter-box ul.first > li", "label": "h4" } },
    { "id": "key-topic",      "name": "Key Discussion Points",           "etId": null,     "repeat": { "item": ".key-topic-card", "label": "h3" } },
    { "id": "our-speakers",   "name": "Our Speakers",                    "etId": null,     "repeat": { "item": ".gridPadItem", "label": "h5" } },
    { "id": "fact-marquee",   "name": "Reasons not to miss",             "etId": null,     "repeat": { "item": ".news-card", "label": ".content h3" } },
    { "id": "conventions-box","name": "Who should attend",               "etId": null,     "repeat": { "item": ".conventions-wdgt ul.first > li", "label": "h3" } },
    { "id": "glimpses_event", "name": "Gallery",                         "etId": null,     "repeat": { "item": ".glimpses-grid > .images__link", "label": "img" } },
    { "id": "contact-us",     "name": "Contact us",                      "etId": null,     "repeat": { "item": ".flex-width-auto > .col-md-4", "label": ".line-1" } },
    { "id": "about-wrapper",  "name": "Manifesto",                       "etId": null }
  ]
}
